    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0561" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg465"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Fava to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Italian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-10-09"><hi rendition="#italic">October 9,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: In your kind note of
                    September 29 you were pleased to confirm the notice previously given me that,
                    according to a communication addressed to you by the private secretary of the
                    governor of Louisiana, the time for the next meeting of the grand jury of
                    Madison Parish is in January, but that it is the intention of the authorities of
                    that parish to call a special meeting before that time, the date of which will
                    be made known as soon as the judge can fix it.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to thank you for this courteous information, which <pb
                        facs="0562" n="466" xml:id="pg466"/> I hastened to communicate to my
                    Government, while awaiting the further information on the subject, which, I
                    doubt not, you will be pleased to send me at the proper time.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fava.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
